  "title": "Village Loom",
  "rules": [
    "Grow flax beside your own plot, cut it with a valid sickle, and gather dye berries. Each material inventory holds at most 2.",
    "Reserve the spinner with 1 fiber, or the loom with 1 yarn and 1 dye while holding a valid shuttle. Each shared facility holds one job or one finished output.",
    "A job needs 2 labor units. Commit beside its facility to work this step and the next; while committed, only Wait is legal.",
    "Helpers can finish another makers reserved job. Only its owner collects the output: yarn at the spinner, cloth at the loom.",
    "Starting a job consumes 1 machine condition. At zero condition work stalls. Spend 1 fiber beside a machine to restore up to 2 condition, capped at 3.",
    "Sickle belongs to role 0 and shuttle to role 1. Owners may lend to an adjacent villager for 8 use steps. An expired tool stays physically with its holder but cannot be used by that borrower.",
    "Return tools beside their owners. Owners may physically reclaim them from adjacent holders, including before a loan expires.",
    "Give fiber, yarn or dye to an adjacent eligible villager. A handoff changes real inventories; it awards no artificial social score.",
    "Sell cloth beside the market. Each of two personal orders earns 3 by your private deadline, otherwise 1. The fair closes at step 80.",
    "Flax stalks, skeins, cloth, machine wear, busy workers and carried tools show actual state. Any legal human action sequence is accepted; scripted examples are unexecuted."
  ],
